This Western blot (Figure 7D) confirms that Nano-11, particularly when combined with LPS priming, induces the secretion of active IL-1β. The blot shows the inactive pro-IL-1β precursor (approximately 30 kD) in cell lysates when LPS is present. More significantly, the active, secreted form of IL-1β, identified at approximately 15 kD to 17 kD, is clearly visible in the supernatant from cells treated with both Nano-11 and LPS. This verifies that the IL-1β detected in ELISA assays is the biologically active form, highlighting Nano-11's ability to trigger pro-inflammatory cytokine processing and release in dendritic cells.